ATTRIBUTION NOTICE

The BFF (Bytewise Function Fields) algorithm and virtual machine instruction set
are based on the research of Agüera y Arcas et al. (arXiv:2406.19108, 2024).
This implementation is an independent GPU port; no original research code was
used or adapted.

The GPU compute shader architecture pattern (C# MonoBehaviour orchestrator +
ScriptableObject settings + ComputeShader kernels + RenderTexture pipeline) was
taken from Sebastian Lague's Slime Simulation (github.com/SebLague/Slime-Simulation,
GPL v3), which was used as a working reference.

Specifically, and as the shader's own comments record: the trail diffuse-and-decay
step (BFFSim.compute:64) follows his implementation closely, the integer hash at
:52-57 uses the same constants, and several identifiers (decayRate, diffuseRate,
TrailMap) are his. The BFF virtual machine, instruction set, replication mechanism
and species dynamics were written from the paper specification, not from his project.

Whether that reuse makes this a derivative work of a GPL-v3 project has not been
assessed by a lawyer, and the MIT grant below should be read with that open. If
you intend to reuse this code, raise an issue first.

The decision to use MIT rather than GPL reflects that this codebase is an original
implementation drawing on published research and common Unity patterns, not a
derivative work of any GPL-licensed software.
